WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
- Today I'm going to answer your questions

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.840
on career and coinciding topics.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.150
On my Instagram channel, Firm Learning,

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.660
I recently asked you

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.270
to submit the questions

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:12.450
that you want to have answered by me.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.580
I already directly answered many of them

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.920
on my Instagram channel,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.220
but still, there were some questions

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.920
that many people asked.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.440
And I want to use this video

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.940
to answer these questions

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.450
for this broader audience

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.160
because I know and I trust

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.520
that many of you guys

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.710
are asking yourself the same questions.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.840
So welcome to another coffee break here

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.750
on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.840
My name is Heinrich,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.720
and here on my channel Firm Learning,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.030
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.060
in the first years of your careers.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.350
So I will now always
read out the questions

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.250
here on my phone.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.330
And the first question is,

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.350
can non native Germans enter
into McKinsey in Germany

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.130
with C1 level German?

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.410
And hear questions like this

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.630
not always I will answer

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.520
with a more general type of approach.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.670
So not talking about specific firms,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.660
but rather, for instance,

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.270
NBB firms in general.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.350
And the answer here is that, yes,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.420
you do not need to be a native German

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.560
to work at a German MBB firm.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.830
And this is true for most other
European countries as well.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.380
Indeed, the two requirements

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.430
that will be required from you,

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.010
are first, that usually you will need

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.960
to have a valid work permit,

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.430
a valid work visa,

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.400
to actually be able to
work in the country.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.610
And second, you will need

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.760
to have local language skills.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.300
So not necessarily on a native level,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.200
but at least on a business
proficiency level.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.030
So C1 should usually qualify for that.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.330
Next question.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:38.350
Is it worth doing an MBA
even though I have a PhD

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.110
and three years of consulting experience?

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.860
And here now I want to generalize this

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.900
to the question,

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.140
is it worth to do an MBA

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.550
especially if you already have lots

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.010
of academic experience?

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.380
And here I'd say it very much depends

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.480
on your goals.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.160
So usually, just to
advance in your career,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.810
I do not think that an MBA

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.480
is necessarily required.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.590
However, an MBA can help us

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.840
to make a transition in your career.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.930
So whenever you feel like you are stuck

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.000
in a specific area

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.950
in your career,

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.580
then the NBA is like the Joker card

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.160
that you can pull out once in your life,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.540
and that can really help you

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.820
to make that transition.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.700
And I already once made
a video about that,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.200
how exactly this works.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.900
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.720
So check it out to learn more about this.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.620
Is it possible

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.850
to get into MBB

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.220
with an extremely low GPA,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.460
and I have three years of experience?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.920
So let's just say it will
be extremely difficult,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.070
especially if your GPA

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.310
is really low.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.100
So I'd say if your GPA may be

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.520
as average but not super stellar,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.190
then it already will be tough.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.970
But probably you can compensate

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.027
that of some other parts of your profile

00:02:44.027 --> 00:02:45.140
and really stand up.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.250
But if your GPA is really low,

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.490
then again, I don't want
to say it's impossible.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.210
Maybe if you're really a genius,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.330
a superstar,

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.120
this comes through to your application

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.000
by other areas of your profile,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.780
then maybe you have a shot.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.880
But for most people,

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.720
I consider it really difficult

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.870
and probably unfortunately not realistic.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.040
How would you go about
getting an internship

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.030
at one of the big four consulting firms?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.580
And here, I don't think there's some kind

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.510
of magic trick that you
need to have, right.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.480
And what you need to understand

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.460
is that these firms

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.210
often have highly professional
recruiting processes.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.310
So while of course,

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.730
it might help if you
already know a consultant,

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.810
and you can then directly forward

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.440
your application to HR,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.830
you should be able to assume

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:24.910
that with these firms,

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.730
you can just apply via the online form

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.010
and your application will
be treated professionally.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.480
And if you fulfill the criteria,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.630
then you will be invited.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.600
And indeed, when I applied to NBB,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.060
I always just used the
regular application form.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.980
I didn't have any insight

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.840
or contacts in these firms.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.610
And this worked out really well for me,

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.370
and it will work for you as well,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.170
if you fulfill of course the criteria.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.590
How hard is it to get

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.480
in McKinsey after your bachelor?

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.080
And indeed not generalizing it,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.680
not for all the NBB firms.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.150
So usually, you can assume

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.470
that if you have a bachelor,

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.930
the hurdles to get in

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.900
are pretty similar

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.450
than if you have a pre-experience master.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.200
Therefore, it can be a bit tougher

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.970
to get in with only a bachelor

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.600
because the criteria
against you are measured

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.180
and very similar compared to

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.570
if you start with a master.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.740
But as it will be one or two years earlier

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.320
in your development both
from the personal side

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.920
that maybe also from the internship

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.007
that you have completed,

00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:18.460
you will need to have achieved more

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.090
in the rather short time
span of the bachelor

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.380
to be invited to the interview

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.213
and then to get in.

00:04:23.213 --> 00:04:24.730
Therefore, it's not impossible.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.190
But yes, I guess you can argue

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.960
that it's a bit more challenging.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.920
Are MBA's mandatory

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.330
to get into MBB?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.280
No, not at all.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.050
This is not at all mandatory.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.470
And especially in countries like Germany,

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.740
MBAs are still quite uncommon.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.930
Just most people don't do an MBA.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.750
So people are regularly hired

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.710
at MBB firms without an MBA.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:45.700
But even in the US

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.077
or other countries where MBAs

00:04:47.077 --> 00:04:48.240
are more common,

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.830
you can absolutely start

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.663
with a bad shot,

00:04:50.663 --> 00:04:51.800
with an undergraduate degree

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.510
in a business analyst position

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.490
and you will get in.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.020
And an MBA by no means

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.050
is a hard requirement.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.130
What is the best book

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.540
that I've read recently?

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.373
So here are

00:05:00.373 --> 00:05:01.206
I can recommend you

00:05:01.206 --> 00:05:02.880
to check out my book recommendations,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.430
you find a link to that below

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.730
in the video description,

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:06.870
there are link to a page

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.730
with all the books

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.290
that I can really recommend.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.123
And of course,

00:05:10.123 --> 00:05:11.510
some of them I've also read recently.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.460
Do you think there might be a valid reason

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.910
to go for Tier Two instead of a Tier One?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:16.743
So here, of course,

00:05:16.743 --> 00:05:18.730
people might have very personal reasons

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.370
to choose certain firms.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.203
And of course,

00:05:21.203 --> 00:05:23.260
personal fit might play a role as well.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.590
But I believe that for most candidates,

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.890
there's not really a reason
why you should join a Tier Two

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.230
if you have the opportunity

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.063
to join a Tier One.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.090
And the reason is that

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.670
in terms of work-life balance,

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.900
in terms of overall working experience,

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:35.930
they are quite similar.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:36.840
But in Tier One firms,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.230
you will often have the opportunity

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.320
to work for slightly more relevant

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.670
and important projects.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.040
Also, the support that you get

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:45.550
via the whole back office
infrastructure is larger,

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.560
so you can focus more as a consultant

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.120
on the key coinciding topics.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.090
And lastly, the brand value for your CV,

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.920
but also your exit opportunities

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:53.810
after your work

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.100
will be slightly better

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.370
in Tier One firms compared

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.210
to Tier Two firms.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.470
This is at least my opinion.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.640
What are the advantages or disadvantages

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.220
of doing a master?

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.080
And here I think the
answer is pretty similar

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.070
to advantages or disadvantages

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.240
of doing an MBA,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.170
and here are also a video
about that about that.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.527
I will link it somewhere here above.

00:06:10.527 --> 00:06:11.840
But in generally the cost

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.490
of doing a master are twofold.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.430
First, it's an investment of time.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.550
And second, it's an investment of money.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:18.550
So you need to ask yourself

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.330
whether these two types of investments

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.163
are worth it.

00:06:21.163 --> 00:06:23.460
Investment of time will
usually be compensated

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.860
if you're able to start one step higher,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.210
if you start in the workforce

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.780
with a master compared to a bachelor.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.570
And at least for the consulting firms,

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.080
this is usually the case,

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.320
usually you start

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.350
one level higher with a master.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.377
And therefore you can compensate

00:06:36.377 --> 00:06:37.960
for the loss of time

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.090
by already being one step further ahead

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.040
in your career journey.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:41.960
Especially if you work

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.280
in a private university,

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.530
you will need to pay student fees.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.550
But then the second factor of it is also

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.100
that in this time,

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.710
you will not earn money,

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.130
So you'll miss the salary.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.810
So this of course can add up

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.070
to quite a high sum.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.260
But again, if the master

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.320
opens up career opportunities for you,

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.920
which might have not been available

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:00.820
with your bachelor,

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.070
or maybe also the knowledge

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.227
that you acquire via your master

00:07:03.227 --> 00:07:04.750
will then really help you

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.630
to be successful in the long term.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.040
And this might easily be over compensated

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.020
throughout the lifespan

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:10.853
of your career.

00:07:10.853 --> 00:07:12.150
So keep these two things in mind.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.380
But my personal opinion is

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.440
that if you do a master

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.040
at a target university

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.340
with good grades,

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.770
usually this will be worth the investment

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.800
in the long term in most cases.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.310
What do I do for a living?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.600
Did I quit consulting?

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.110
And if Yes, why?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.710
So yes, I quit consulting
about a year ago,

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:29.900
I worked with McKinsey,

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.040
but now left the firm since then.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.240
And the reasons I
detailed in another video

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.910
where I talk about what things are

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:37.890
that I didn't learn in consulting,

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.820
and I will also link it somewhere above.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.750
So overall, I'm super grateful

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.000
and thankful for former time at MBB.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.990
It was an amazing experience.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:46.910
And I do believe

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.150
that consulting is a great career choice

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.210
for many young business
graduates out there.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.020
But still I felt that after these years

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.860
I wanted to do something
slightly more operationally.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.250
So I joined a German retail company

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.710
